    <statement><p>Find an equation for the paraboloid <m>z = x^{2}+y^{2}</m> in spherical
coordinates.  (Enter rho, phi and theta for <m>\rho</m>, <m>\phi</m>
and <m>\theta</m>, respectively.)</p>
<p>equation: <fillin characters="55" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>rho = \frac{\cos\mathopen{}\left(phi\right)}{\sin^{2}\mathopen{}\left(phi\right)}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>rho = \frac{\cos\mathopen{}\left(phi\right)}{\sin^{2}\mathopen{}\left(phi\right)}</m>.



</solution>
